# Azure App Service (Linux custom container) portal SSH console configuration.
#
# Reference documents (https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/configure-custom-container?tabs=debian&pivots=container-linux)
#
# Important:
# - This is NOT intended for exposing SSH to the public internet.
# - App Service portal SSH expects sshd to listen on port 2222.
# - The Ciphers/MACs lists must include at least one compatible legacy option for the portal SSH feature.
# - Root login is enabled to support the portal SSH workflow (root password is set to 'Docker!' in Dockerfile per App Service requirement).
#
# If you publish port 2222 externally (e.g., with docker run -p 2222:2222), you MUST revisit these settings.
Port 2222
ListenAddress 0.0.0.0
LoginGraceTime 180
X11Forwarding yes

# Must include at least one of: aes128-cbc, 3des-cbc, aes256-cbc
Ciphers chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com,aes256-gcm@openssh.com,aes128-gcm@openssh.com,aes256-ctr,aes192-ctr,aes128-ctr,aes128-cbc

# Must include at least one of: hmac-sha1, hmac-sha1-96
MACs hmac-sha2-512-etm@openssh.com,hmac-sha2-256-etm@openssh.com,hmac-sha2-512,hmac-sha2-256,hmac-sha1

StrictModes yes
SyslogFacility DAEMON
PasswordAuthentication yes
PermitEmptyPasswords no
PermitRootLogin yes
Subsystem sftp internal-sftp
